{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["The sense of <b>you shall not wrong one another</b> is a warning to the seller, for the first [verse] refers to the buyer." "<b>For I am YHWH your Elohim.</b> And since I am your Elohim, I exact payment from both [parties] — from whoever wrongs his fellow. And if you keep My statutes, the land will yield its produce; and the reason to mention this is on account of the count of produce."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:19.936758263Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}